Panics if called from a panicking thread.

# Examples

The following will print the custom message, and then the normal output of panic.

```should_panic
#![feature(panic_update_hook)]
use std::panic;

// Equivalent to
// let prev = panic::take_hook();
// panic::set_hook(move |info| {
//     println!("...");
//     prev(info);
// );
