10837.docs:
Exact shift left. Computes `self << rhs` as long as it can be reversed losslessly.

Returns `None` if any bits that would be shifted out differ from the resulting sign bit
or if `rhs` >=
`i128::BITS`.
Otherwise, returns `Some(self << rhs)`.

# Examples

```
#![feature(exact_bitshifts)]

assert_eq!(0x1i128.exact_shl(4), Some(0x10));
assert_eq!(0x1i128.exact_shl(i128::BITS - 2), Some(1 << i128::BITS - 2));
assert_eq!(0x1i128.exact_shl(i128::BITS - 1), None);
assert_eq!((-0x2i128).exact_shl(i128::BITS - 2), Some(-0x2 << i128::BITS - 2));
assert_eq!((-0x2i128).exact_shl(i128::BITS - 1), None);
```

